<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-persimilis-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Schnakenberg critical wavelength for Drosophila persimilis at 2.1 µm — MorphoEval overall 77.3/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Pass 1. Focal wavelength is the assigned 2.098 µm detail tier at 0 Ma. Predecessor D. paulistorum and successor D. planitibia change only the diffusion length, λ ∝ L^0.42. Self-test reports Pearson r = 0.9993 on the Du sweep, ablation ratio 0.051, and stripe order paulistorum < persimilis < planitibia. Full credit is withheld: the gallery plate is not an electron micrograph, β is a transfer, and the critical mode is seeded. Overall 77.3/100 (faithfulness 73.9, reproducibility 85.5); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 6c49ecbdcc1e6d2fcf72d168ee46196263be7d3b; environment: . Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 84, Morphological realism / specimen match 68, Parameter expressivity 74, Morphometric validation 70, Source and data traceability 90, Code-to-model traceability 82, Reproducibility package 84. Output judged: docs/media/drosophila_persimilis_turing_wavelength_s0_comparison.png: rendered output of models/2026-delphi10000-drosophila-persimilis-turing-wavelength-s0.py at 6c49ecbdcc1e6d2fcf72d168ee46196263be7d3b, image/png, 306753 B, 1440×960 px, artifact_sha256 dedf562e5c821cfda99a468d5b61d22be7bdf2ffbf87a1a4b3f9ad686681793a (sha256 dedf562e5c821cfda99a468d5b61d22be7bdf2ffbf87a1a4b3f9ad686681793a), spec_fingerprint 6cfd22b3b1eb8b085833af27f643b5e89f6fcf635888d87c45635473a8295900. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: 6cfd22b3b1eb8b085833af27f643b5e89f6fcf635888d87c45635473a8295900; artifact_sha256: dedf562e5c821cfda99a468d5b61d22be7bdf2ffbf87a1a4b3f9ad686681793a; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/drosophila_persimilis_turing_wavelength_s0/drosophila_persimilis_specimen.jpg=f1216712eddebdcd..., datasets/drosophila_persimilis_turing_wavelength_s0/drosophila_persimilis_turing_wavelength_s0_reference.json=a12c3e1298940f01..., datasets/drosophila_persimilis_turing_wavelength_s0/paper_citations.bib=9eb570b42e0a0ddc...}. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Noor et al. 2001: chromosomal inversions contribute to reproductive isolation between D. pseudoobscura and D. persimilis. | Dobzhansky & Spassky 1959: D. paulistorum is a cluster of incipient species. | Kambysellis et al. 1995: Hawaiian Drosophila, including the picture-wing radiation that contains D. planitibia, diversified by ecological shifts. | Turing 1952 and Schnakenberg 1979: a diffusion-driven instability selects a finite critical wavenumber. | Ready, Hanson & Benzer 1976: the Drosophila retina is a neurocrystalline lattice, which is the motive for a roughly 2 µm period.; reconstructed_in_script: Schnakenberg Jacobian, onset wavenumber k_c^2 = (D_v f_u + D_u g_v) / (2 D_u D_v), and λ = 2π/k_c tuned to 2.098 µm at diffusion ratio 20. | Allometric map λ = 2.098 µm * (L/2.82 mm)^0.42 using catalog body lengths 2.36, 2.82 and 5.30 mm. | Equal-diffusion ablation, five-point Du sweep, five-seed SD, N=64 vs N=96 convergence, and β-endpoint integrations.; transfer_boundary: 2.098 µm is the assigned tier-3 detail wavelength for this slot, not a measurement printed in Noor et al. 2001. | β = 0.42 is a scale-transfer exponent for subcellular diffusion length, not a regression on pigment periods of these three species.; does_not_claim: Does not claim the species-gallery spiral is a micrograph of 2.1 µm pigment granules. | Does not claim broadband noise selects k_c inside 1200 steps. | Does not claim the 117 µm primordium slot (2891) parameters.." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: {'id': 'R1', 'item': 'The gallery plate is not a 2.1 µm micrograph. Keep the orientation KS between the plate and the activator field as a separate metric, and do not read the GIF terminal-frame similarity as ultrastructural agreement.'}",
        "remediation needed: {'id': 'R2', 'item': 'β = 0.42 is a transfer. Credit the integrated β=0.20 and β=0.70 endpoints only after the self-test order check is re-run and the gap is reported against the analytic gap without copying it.'}",
        "remediation needed: {'id': 'R3', 'item': 'The critical mode is seeded. The equal-diffusion ablation must stay in the scored measurement set so the stripe is not credited as an imposed drawing. A noise-selected transient is still not shown.'}" ;
    pk:hasScore 7.73e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "mostly faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-persimilis-turing-wavelength-s0-parameter-expressivity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Schnakenberg critical wavelength for Drosophila persimilis at 2.1 µm — Parameter expressivity: 74/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "The Du sweep is monotonic and the analytic β table keeps paulistorum shorter than planitibia from β=0.20 to 0.70. Endpoint diffusivities are integrated, but this first reading does not yet treat that grid as a full substitute for a measured wavelength series." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-parameter-expressivity> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/parameter-expressivity" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-persimilis-turing-wavelength-s0-parameter-expressivity-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-persimilis-turing-wavelength-s0-parameter-expressivity-2> ;
    pk:hasScore 7.4e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "mostly faithful" .

