<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-persimilis-turing-wavelength-s0-specimen-match> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Schnakenberg critical wavelength for Drosophila persimilis at 2.1 µm — Morphological realism / specimen match: 68/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "The comparison figure places the gallery plate beside three stripe fields whose spacing increases from paulistorum to planitibia. The plate is a golden-brown spiral, explicitly captioned as not an electron micrograph. The growth GIF's last frame is that plate, so a high computer-vision score against it is expected and is not ultrastructural agreement." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-specimen-match> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/specimen-match" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-persimilis-turing-wavelength-s0-specimen-match-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-persimilis-turing-wavelength-s0-specimen-match-2> ;
    pk:hasScore 6.8e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "mostly faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-persimilis-turing-wavelength-s0> a pk:Claim ;
    rdfs:label "Schnakenberg critical wavelength for Drosophila persimilis at 2.1 µm (Drosophila persimilis)",
        "Schnakenberg critical wavelength for Drosophila persimilis at 2.1 µm faithfully reproduces Drosophila persimilis morphology" ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-drosophila-persimilis-turing-wavelength-s0-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-drosophila-persimilis-turing-wavelength-s0-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-drosophila-persimilis-turing-wavelength-s0-3> ;
    dct:description "The simulation script(s) models/2026-delphi10000-drosophila-persimilis-turing-wavelength-s0.py implement the cited source model as published and produce forms that match real Drosophila persimilis specimens and the source authors' figures. A belief under audit, not a fact: its credibility is carried by the MorphoEval rubric assessments." ;
    dct:subject <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-delphi10000-drosophila-persimilis-turing-wavelength-s0.py> ;
    schema:about "Drosophila persimilis" ;
    schema:additionalProperty "does_not_claim: Does not claim broadband noise selects k_c inside 1200 steps.",
        "does_not_claim: Does not claim the 117 µm primordium slot (2891) parameters.",
        "does_not_claim: Does not claim the species-gallery spiral is a micrograph of 2.1 µm pigment granules.",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Allometric map λ = 2.098 µm * (L/2.82 mm)^0.42 using catalog body lengths 2.36, 2.82 and 5.30 mm.",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Equal-diffusion ablation, five-point Du sweep, five-seed SD, N=64 vs N=96 convergence, and β-endpoint integrations.",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Schnakenberg Jacobian, onset wavenumber k_c^2 = (D_v f_u + D_u g_v) / (2 D_u D_v), and λ = 2π/k_c tuned to 2.098 µm at diffusion ratio 20.",
        "reported_in_source: Dobzhansky & Spassky 1959: D. paulistorum is a cluster of incipient species.",
        "reported_in_source: Kambysellis et al. 1995: Hawaiian Drosophila, including the picture-wing radiation that contains D. planitibia, diversified by ecological shifts.",
        "reported_in_source: Noor et al. 2001: chromosomal inversions contribute to reproductive isolation between D. pseudoobscura and D. persimilis.",
        "reported_in_source: Ready, Hanson & Benzer 1976: the Drosophila retina is a neurocrystalline lattice, which is the motive for a roughly 2 µm period.",
        "reported_in_source: Turing 1952 and Schnakenberg 1979: a diffusion-driven instability selects a finite critical wavenumber.",
        "transfer_boundary: 2.098 µm is the assigned tier-3 detail wavelength for this slot, not a measurement printed in Noor et al. 2001.",
        "transfer_boundary: β = 0.42 is a scale-transfer exponent for subcellular diffusion length, not a regression on pigment periods of these three species." ;
    pk:anatomicalStructure "Turing pigment stripe / ocellus wavelength in Drosophila persimilis (Pacific Coast Sister Obscura Fly)" ;
    pk:aristotelianEfficientCause "1. Chemical Turing / RD" ;
    pk:aristotelianMegistonGenos "II. Anaima (Invertebrata)" ;
    pk:aristotelianPoionForm "Stripes, Spots & Ocelli" ;
    pk:aristotelianPosonLaw "Turing Wavenumber k_c" ;
    pk:aristotelianSubalternClass "Entoma (Arthropoda)" ;
    pk:biologicalGenus "Drosophila" ;
    pk:context "script(s): https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-delphi10000-drosophila-persimilis-turing-wavelength-s0.py; output: docs/media/drosophila_persimilis_turing_wavelength_s0_comparison.png; organism: Drosophila persimilis; environment: n/a; claim_boundary: [reported_in_source: Noor et al. 2001: chromosomal inversions contribute to reproductive isolation between D. pseudoobscura and D. persimilis. | Dobzhansky & Spassky 1959: D. paulistorum is a cluster of incipient species. | Kambysellis et al. 1995: Hawaiian Drosophila, including the picture-wing radiation that contains D. planitibia, diversified by ecological shifts. | Turing 1952 and Schnakenberg 1979: a diffusion-driven instability selects a finite critical wavenumber. | Ready, Hanson & Benzer 1976: the Drosophila retina is a neurocrystalline lattice, which is the motive for a roughly 2 µm period.; reconstructed_in_script: Schnakenberg Jacobian, onset wavenumber k_c^2 = (D_v f_u + D_u g_v) / (2 D_u D_v), and λ = 2π/k_c tuned to 2.098 µm at diffusion ratio 20. | Allometric map λ = 2.098 µm * (L/2.82 mm)^0.42 using catalog body lengths 2.36, 2.82 and 5.30 mm. | Equal-diffusion ablation, five-point Du sweep, five-seed SD, N=64 vs N=96 convergence, and β-endpoint integrations.; transfer_boundary: 2.098 µm is the assigned tier-3 detail wavelength for this slot, not a measurement printed in Noor et al. 2001. | β = 0.42 is a scale-transfer exponent for subcellular diffusion length, not a regression on pigment periods of these three species.; does_not_claim: Does not claim the species-gallery spiral is a micrograph of 2.1 µm pigment granules. | Does not claim broadband noise selects k_c inside 1200 steps. | Does not claim the 117 µm primordium slot (2891) parameters.]; phenomenon_size: 1.9 µm (1.919e-06 m, log10=-5.717 m, tier=3_subcellular_um); species_scale_ladder (10 runs from 1.9 µm to 4.3 mm): 1.9 µm:drosophila-affinis-bioelectric-polarity, 6.0 µm:drosophila-affinis-vertex-packing, 96 µm:drosophila-affinis-turing-wavelength, 192 µm:drosophila-affinis-clock-wavefront, 432 µm:drosophila-affinis-morphogen-condensation, 528 µm:drosophila-affinis-elastic-buckling, 600 µm:drosophila-affinis-flux-canalization, 840 µm:drosophila-affinis-branching-tree" ;
